# stores.rec: the town's shops and services, one record per stock or menu. A record either names its items (a
# list) or filters the whole items.rec table (Diablo's shops); several records may share an npc, whose menu is
# their services and whose stock their rolls, in file order.
# Who and what:
#   internal_name     the record's id
#   npc               the townsperson (internal name) it belongs to; repeatable (shopkeepers sharing one stock)
#   stock             how it stocks: smith, premium, witch, healer, boy (Diablo's rolls) or list; none: sells nothing
#   buys              what it buys from the hero: smith, witch, hellfire_smith, hellfire_witch or any; none: nothing
#   service           a menu entry: buy buy_basic buy_premium sell repair recharge identify heal heal_on_visit donate
#                     peek stash transfer, some with an argument, e.g. identify(100); repeatable
#   when              a quest condition (quests.rec's language) for the record to count at all
# A list:
#   always / sometimes   an item (internal_name) always / possibly in stock; repeatable
#   item_count        how many items it stocks, "min-max", the always items included
#   sometimes_count   how many of the sometimes items, "min-max"
#   turnover_items    items replaced each time the hero comes back
#   purse             gold it has for buying from the hero
# A filter (empty: no opinion):
#   types / exclude_types   item types: misc sword axe bow mace shield larmor helm marmor harmor staff gold ring
#                     amulet food
#   misc_ids / exclude_misc_ids   IMISC_ kinds; exclude_spells SPL_ names; exclude_charged_types types whose
#                     spell-carrying items it won't stock; items: named items that are in regardless
#   min_dlvl_divisor  n: an item must also be at least (level)/n deep
#   max_value         an item worth more is rolled again (0: no cap); tries: n rolls to fit the hero, then settle
#   double_drops      true: IDROP_DOUBLE items count twice
#   slot_levels       a premium stock's fixed slots, each an item level offset; rotate_by: slots it shifts each level
#   featured_misc_id / featured_count   a kind of item put out first, and how many
#   shuns "<class internal_name> <type> ..." types it keeps away from a class (repeatable); shun_tries how long it tries
#   usable_elixirs_only   only elixirs of a stat still under the class maximum
#   recharge_uniques  recharges unique items too
#   price_adjust      +1/n or -1/n: sells at value plus or minus value/n
#
# Diablo's town vendors in the unified stores.rec schema every mod uses (see defs.Vendor).
# Ports 1.09's SpawnSmith/SpawnPremium/SpawnWitch/SpawnHealer/SpawnBoy: where Heaven&Hell names the
# items a vendor sells, Diablo names the criteria and rolls the whole item table through them. Both are the
# one record; these vendors just use its filter half.
#
# npc is who runs it, stock the engine's stock strategy, buys what it takes off the hero, service each entry
# of the NPC's menu (see defs.VendorServices), when a quest condition for the record to count at all.
#
# item_count is the stock roll inclusive of both ends, the always items included (SpawnSmith's random_(50, 10) + 10
# and so on). max_value is STORE_MAX_VALUE / BOY_MAX_VALUE: an item worth more is rolled again.
# Hellfire's store options (tries, shuns, featured_*, usable_elixirs_only, recharge_uniques, the hellfire_* buy
# rules) are left unset: this is 1.09.

# Griswold's premium stock rolls before his basic stock (SetupTownStores' order) and is listed after it.
internal_name: premium
npc: griswold
stock: premium
max_value: 140000
min_dlvl_divisor: 4
exclude_types: misc gold staff
slot_levels: -1 -1 0 0 1 2
rotate_by: 2

internal_name: smith
npc: griswold
stock: smith
buys: smith
service: buy_basic
service: buy_premium
service: sell
service: repair
item_count: 10-19
max_value: 140000
double_drops: true
exclude_types: misc gold staff ring amulet

internal_name: witch
npc: adria
stock: witch
buys: witch
service: buy
service: sell
service: recharge
item_count: 10-17
max_value: 140000
always: potion_of_mana
always: potion_of_full_mana
always: scroll_of_town_portal
types: misc staff
exclude_misc_ids: IMISC_MANA IMISC_FULLMANA IMISC_HEAL IMISC_FULLHEAL
exclude_spells: SPL_TOWN SPL_RESURRECT SPL_HEALOTHER

# Pepin: "Receive healing" is an entry of his menu (S_StartHealer).
internal_name: healer
npc: pepin
stock: healer
service: heal
service: buy
item_count: 10-17
always: potion_of_healing
always: potion_of_full_healing
types: misc
misc_ids: IMISC_ELIXSTR IMISC_ELIXMAG IMISC_ELIXDEX IMISC_ELIXVIT IMISC_REJUV IMISC_FULLREJUV
items: scroll_of_healing

# Wirt: 50 gold to look, and his item costs half again its value.
internal_name: boy
npc: wirt
stock: boy
service: peek(50)
max_value: 90000
price_adjust: +1/2
exclude_types: misc gold staff

# Cain identifies for a flat 100 gold (AddStoreHoldId), and sells nothing.
internal_name: story
npc: cain
service: identify(100)
